content.thinking:
- Modern yapf_rail.cpp has NO `_debug_desync_level` or `DEBUG(desync, ...)` — so decouple's desync-check pattern doesn't exist in modern yapf_rail.cpp (modern YAPF uses a different desync-check mechanism — maybe in the base class or via different means). I'll simplify stFindNearestCoupleTrain: remove the dual-run desync check, just run once:
```cpp
	static Trackdir stFindNearestCoupleTrain(const Train *v, bool dont_reserve)
	{
		/* Create pathfinder instance */
		Tpf pf1;
		pf1.DisableCache(true);
		return pf1.FindNearestCoupleTrain(v, dont_reserve);
	}
```

- TeleportCost call: `if (has_parent && n.flags_u.flags_s.teleport) { extra_cost += Yapf().TeleportCost(n.GetLastTile(), n.parent->GetLastTile()); }` — teleport flag for stations. My CYapfDestinationTrainRailT needs TeleportCost. Return 0 (couple approach has no teleport). Signature: `int TeleportCost(TileIndex cur_tile, TileIndex prev_tile)` — wait it's called with 2 args here (n.GetLastTile(), n.parent->GetLastTile()). Add to CYapfDestinationTrainRailT:
```cpp
	inline int TeleportCost(TileIndex cur_tile, TileIndex prev_tile)
	{
		return 0;
	}
```

- CountVehiclesInChain: add `#include "../../vehicle_func.h"` to yapf_destrail.hpp.

Let me apply these 3 fixes.

