Modern CmdModifyOrder is quite different but the structure is similar (switch on order type for validation, switch on mof for data validation, then the apply switch). I need to add:

1. In the order-type validation switch: `case OT_GOTO_COUPLE: if (mof != MOF_COUPLE_LOAD && mof != MOF_COUPLE_CARGO && mof != MOF_COUPLE_VALUE) return CMD_ERROR; break;` and `case OT_DECOUPLE: if (mof != MOF_FIRST_ORDERS && mof != MOF_SECOND_ORDERS && mof != MOF_DECOUPLE_VALUE) return CMD_ERROR; break;`
2. In the mof data-validation switch: add cases MOF_SECOND_ORDERS/MOF_FIRST_ORDERS (train + data<ODOF_END), MOF_DECOUPLE (train + nonstop check), MOF_DECOUPLE_VALUE (data<=127), MOF_COUPLE_LOAD (data<ODC_END), MOF_COUPLE_CARGO (cargo validation), MOF_COUPLE_VALUE (data<=127).
3. In the apply switch: MOF_DECOUPLE_VALUE/MOF_DECOUPLE/MOF_COUPLE_LOAD/MOF_COUPLE_CARGO/MOF_COUPLE_VALUE/MOF_FIRST_ORDERS/MOF_SECOND_ORDERS cases.

